{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1120323,"num_turns":113,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"96f66f28-8007-4367-b2f3-9dc6db60f162","total_cost_usd":7.784634500000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152814,"cache_read_input_tokens":9096187,"output_tokens":68191,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":152814,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1227,"cache_read_input_tokens":171566,"cache_creation_input_tokens":646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":646},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2696,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.002806,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":164,"outputTokens":68191,"cacheReadInputTokens":9096187,"cacheCreationInputTokens":152814,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":7.781828500000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Review complete. **Verdict: changes requested** — `BUG-260802-1s021p` routed to `to-dev`.\n\n## Blocking defect\n\nThe head commit's Windows portability fix repairs **one of five identical call sites**. `6e7742f` added `_utime_portably()` and rewrote old line 2967 → new 2989 in `tests/protocol_lifecycle_observations.py`. Four identical unguarded calls survive at lines **3055, 3063, 3071, 3112**, all inside the same `_observe_gc` (def 2751), all *after* the repaired one — previously unreachable only because execution died at 2967 first.\n\nReachability verified rather than assumed:\n- No `os.name` / `sys.platform` / `skip` gate anywhere in lines 2780–3120; 2999–3055 is straight-line code with no `try`/`except` covering the span.\n- `_observe_gc` demonstrably runs on `windows-latest` — the prior run's traceback is inside this function.\n- The active `os.utime` monkeypatch (line 638 → `observed_os_utime`, 582–605) forwards `follow_symlinks` verbatim to the real function, so `NotImplementedError` propagates.\n\nPrior run 30737293076 failed windows×4 with exactly `NotImplementedError: utime: follow_symlinks unavailable on this platform` at line 2967 — genuine `Run tests` failures, not cancellations. Because all 32 lifecycle cases draw from one shared cached observation build, that single raise fails the whole lifecycle suite.\n\nThe in-flight run at head has ubuntu×4, macos×4 and `mypy strict` green; windows×4 still running (~2h50m; prior Windows jobs took ~2h56m). I predicted failure at line 3055 — falsifiable, but the static evidence stands on its own, so I routed rather than burn another hour of RC time.\n\n## Audited sound — no rework needed\n\n- **Transaction-recovery relocation.** Dry-run stays mutation-free: the removed `if not options.dry_run` guard is subsumed by the pre-existing dry-run early return, which fires before the `ManagerHomeLock`/`recover` block. Recovery-induced drift raises `concurrent_state_change` and is retried (`attempts=3`).\n- **Lock semantics.** `except locking.LockError: raise` restores the pre-existing `EXIT_LOCK` contract that moving the home lock into the commit phase would have swallowed into a generic per-project failure.\n- **New security guard.** `status._runtime_exposes_build_roots` fails closed, and its path matches the installer/gc materialization layout exactly — the main fail-open risk, and it holds. `build_roots` validation already blocks traversal.\n- **Release guards.** `ci.yml` untouched. The PR-body ref `432eb2e` vs CI-pinned `0c81c1f` discrepancy is cosmetic — I verified both carry an identical `conformance/v1` tree `36287c9` and the same manifest digest.\n- **Anti-vacuity.** Every patched seam is a spy delegating to the real implementation, and the suite includes meta-tests that police its own harness (AST scan of hardcoded literals; a forbidden-lossy-proxy scan).\n\nRecommended alongside the fix: extend that existing source-scan pattern to fail if `follow_symlinks=False` appears outside `_utime_portably` — fixing one call site per ~3h Windows round is the actual cost driver here.\n\nEvidence in board resource `BUG-260802-1s021p_pr19-independent-review.md`, board notes, and a `LOGBOOK.md` entry. No code modified.","ttft_ms":1891,"ttft_stream_ms":1376,"time_to_request_ms":166,"type":"result","duration_ms":1166644,"uuid":"1ac48265-f7ed-4315-95df-7e06ac1f8dc0"}
